    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` following the spec, and wrote 49 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 49. The first run had 4 failures, all from my own wrong expectations for the oversize tests: I had used 120×10×10 parcels, whose volumetric weight bills at 2.5 kg, not 1 kg. I changed those tests to 1×1 cross-sections, and the implementation was not changed. The code converts inputs through `str()` for floats, rejects `bool` and other types with `TypeError`, validates zone and value ranges with `ValueError`, rounds billable weight up to 0.5 kg, applies the zone factor, free shipping and oversize surcharge in the spec's order, and quantizes once at the end with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. One choice beyond the spec: NaN and infinite numbers raise `ValueError`, since the spec does not cover them. I did not create any files outside `solution.py` and `tests/`, and I installed nothing.",
